TITLE:: FxChainPanel
summary:: a chain's effects, one at a time under a tab each
categories:: Libraries>ParaEQ
related:: Classes/FxChain, Classes/FxChainGUI, Classes/ParaEQPanel, Classes/CompressorPanel

DESCRIPTION::
The chain's row - power, its name and bus, the chain presets, a button per effect
class that is installed and a menu of sc fx kit's effects - then a tab per effect,
in the order the sound goes through them, left to right, and under the tabs the
panel of the effect chosen: the same panel its own window shows. One at a time,
because an effect's panel is a whole device - a display and its cards - and two of
them no longer stack in one window. A tab whose effect is off is dim.

strong::earlier:: and strong::later:: move the effect shown one place along the
chain, strong::remove:: takes it out. The panel follows the chain: an effect added
from code turns up and is shown, one removed goes away, and the effect shown stays
shown when the chain moves it. Only the shown effect's panel runs its analysis.

code::
(
c = FxChain.master;
w = Window("chain", Rect(100, 100, 1000, 620)).front;
p = FxChainPanel(c);
h = FxHintBar();
w.layout = VLayout(p.view, h.view);
p.hints = h;
p.running = true;             // the analysis of the effect shown
w.onClose = { p.remove };
);
p.shown = 1;                  // the second effect
::

link::Classes/ServerPanel:: opens it from its fx button; link::Classes/FxChainGUI::
puts it in a window.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: chain
ARGUMENT:: parent

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: chain
METHOD:: view
METHOD:: panels
The effects' panels, in order.
METHOD:: shown
Which effect is shown, by its place in the chain.
METHOD:: shownPanel
The panel of the effect shown, or nil.
METHOD:: running
Whether the effect shown runs its analysis; the others never do.
METHOD:: hints
METHOD:: refresh
METHOD:: remove
